  "repoURL": "git@github.com:agh-alice/datalake-v2.git",
  "drySha": "d140271df4380ce8e0cea5284ed730e32733eb3f",
  "author": "groundnuty <groundnuty@gmail.com>",
  "date": "2026-08-07T15:33:02Z",
  "subject": "fix: repoint ExternalSecrets to the tenant-writable datalake store",
  "body": "The platform's original ClusterSecretStore `platform` (remoteNamespace\neso-secret-source) is read-only to us. The platform team has created a\nsecond ClusterSecretStore, `datalake` (remoteNamespace\neso-secret-source-datalake, namespaceSelector tenant=datalake, verified\nValid live 2026-08-07), reading a namespace this repo can write.\n\nRepoints secretStoreRef.name: platform -> datalake in all three tier\ncharts' ExternalSecret templates (lakekeeper-pg-encryption, landing-ro,\ningest-env). Same remote keys, same properties -- only the store target\nchanges. The name is hardcoded independently in each of the three\ntemplates (not templated through a shared value), so this is three\nseparate edits, not one -- drift risk noted, not addressed here.\n\nkind's own ClusterSecretStore mirrors prod's under the same name by\ndesign (environments/kind/infra/cluster-secret-store.yaml) -- renamed\nplatform -> datalake there too, plus the two hack/kind-{up,verify}.sh\ngates that assert on that name by literal string, so the mirror keeps\nmirroring. kind's remoteNamespace (eso-secret-source) is left as-is --\nonly the ClusterSecretStore's own name is what the shared chart\ntemplates reference. Applied directly to the running kind cluster via\nkubectl (this file isn't ArgoCD-managed) before this push, so kind's\nApplications re-hydrating against the new secretStoreRef.name don't hit\na missing store and trigger deletionPolicy: Delete on the target\nSecrets.\n\nAlso provisions the one secret with no external dependency:\nlakekeeper-pg-encryption's encryptionKey, generated with openssl rand\n-hex 32 (matching the format hack/kind-up.sh already exercises against\na running Lakekeeper) and created directly in eso-secret-source-datalake\non the tenant cluster. Never rotate this key -- catalog credentials\nencrypted under it become unreadable if it changes.\n\nlanding-ro and ingest-env are untouched beyond the store repoint: the\nPostgres DB they'd need still can't start (cinder-perf quota exhausted,\nPVCs Pending) and S3 credentials aren't available yet.\n\nBlast radius on the live cluster: three secretStoreRef.name fields plus\none new Kubernetes Secret. Everything else in this diff is comments.\n"
}
